# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/slice_2b.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event evo_first_spark
# en: The First Spark
title [5b0523] = 第一缕火花
# en: Evocation I begins with a single instruction from the lectern: "Make heat. Not fire. Heat." Half the class makes nothing. One student makes a small, apologetic fire.
text [db1b7b] = 塑能术 I 以讲台上的一句指令开场：“造热。不是火。是热。”半个班什么都没造出来。有一个学生造出了一小团满怀歉意的火。
# en: A lecture hall with scorch marks on every desk, students holding their palms up as if testing for rain.
scene [47f33f] = 每张课桌上都有焦痕的讲堂，学生们摊开手掌，像在试探下没下雨。
# en: Aim for heat, carefully
opt.left.label [ac4d80] = 小心地只求热
# en: Your palm warms like a stone left in the sun. The lecturer nods, which is better than most get.
opt.left.say.1 [fe739e] = 你的掌心暖得像晒过太阳的石头。讲师点了点头，这已经胜过大多数人了。
# en: Aim for fire, boldly
opt.right.label [639beb] = 大胆地求火
# en: A neat little flame, exactly where you meant it. The lecturer writes your name down. Approvingly, you hope.
opt.right.say.1 [013ce4] = 一小簇利落的火苗，正好出现在你想要的位置。讲师记下了你的名字。你希望是带着赞许的。
# en: Your sleeve learns more about fire than you do. The lecture continues around the smell.
opt.right.say.2 [090858] = 你的袖子比你更懂火了。课在这股焦味里继续。

@event evo_puddle_drill
# en: Puddle Drill
title [3a9384] = 水洼操练
# en: Tidecalling half of the course: a puddle each, and the task of making it stand up and stay up. Yours trembles, considers it, and lies back down.
text [4ca6c9] = 课程的唤潮术部分：每人一个水洼，任务是让它站起来并保持站立。你的那个颤了颤，考虑了一下，又躺了回去。
# en: Students crouched over puddles in a stone courtyard, trying to make the water stand up.
scene [83fa0c] = 学生们蹲在石砌庭院的水洼前，试图让水站起来。
# en: Practise until it stands
opt.left.label [1dfa4e] = 练到它站起来
# en: By the end of the hour your puddle stands like a sulky child. It counts.
opt.left.say.1 [106f8b] = 一节课快结束时，你的水洼像个赌气的孩子一样站着。算数。
# en: Copy the student next to you
opt.right.label [ead31d] = 照搬旁边同学的做法
# en: You learn their trick, and also that they hum while they cast. You hum too. It works, inexplicably.
opt.right.say.1 [c0e062] = 你学到了对方的诀窍，还发现他们施法时会哼歌。你也哼了。莫名其妙地，管用。

@event evo_misfire
# en: Misfire
title [3350b4] = 失手
# en: Someone's tidecalling meets someone else's flame in the middle of the room. The hall fills with scalding steam and twenty students who all have opinions.
text [e661e8] = 某人的唤潮术在房间正中撞上了另一个人的火焰。讲堂里灌满了滚烫的蒸汽，还有二十个各有意见的学生。
# en: A lecture hall filling with steam after a spell meets a bucket of water at the wrong moment.
scene [ffbe1f] = 一道咒语在错误的时刻撞上一桶水，讲堂里蒸汽弥漫。
# en: Shield the front row
opt.left.label [1e4bc0] = 护住前排
# en: You take the worst of it on your sleeves. The front row looks at you the way people look at lifeboats.
opt.left.say.1 [d4298c] = 最烫的那一下你用袖子挡了。前排的人看你的眼神，就像看救生艇。
# en: Get out and open the windows
opt.right.label [eb7ddc] = 出去开窗
# en: The steam pours out into the courtyard and becomes, briefly, a very small cloud with a grudge.
opt.right.say.1 [3f970d] = 蒸汽涌进庭院，短暂地变成了一朵很小、很记仇的云。

@event evo_tide_wall
# en: The Tide Wall
title [f1844c] = 潮墙
# en: Evocation II takes the class to the lakeshore. The exercise: raise a wall of water and hold it while a classmate walks past behind it. Your classmate looks nervous. So do you.
text [5eb5bd] = 塑能术 II 把全班带到湖岸。练习：升起一道水墙并撑住，让一位同学从墙后走过。那位同学看起来很紧张。你也是。
# en: A student holding back a wall of lake water on the shore while classmates watch from behind them.
scene [23ccc0] = 一名学生在岸边挡住一道湖水筑成的墙，同学们在后面看着。
# en: Hold it steady
opt.left.label [d6f0e9] = 稳稳撑住
# en: The wall holds. Your classmate walks past dry and amazed. You let it down gently, which is the hard part.
opt.left.say.1 [240cd4] = 水墙撑住了。同学干干爽爽地走过去，满脸惊叹。你把墙轻轻放下——这才是最难的部分。
# en: The wall holds until it doesn't. Your classmate is very wet and very gracious about it.
opt.left.say.2 [b2a1a9] = 水墙撑住了，直到撑不住。同学浑身湿透，却对此十分大度。
# en: Ask to go second
opt.right.label [208e6d] = 请求第二个上
# en: You watch three people do it first and learn from all of their mistakes.
opt.right.say.1 [2b89b8] = 你看着三个人先做，把他们的错误统统学了个遍。

@event evo_lattice
# en: The Flame Lattice
title [7d30cd] = 火焰格网
# en: Fire woven into a lattice, each strand holding the others up. The lecturer says the founders built wards like this. The lecturer also says you have twenty minutes.
text [954a4b] = 火被编成格网，每一股都撑着其他几股。讲师说创始者当年就是这样筑护界的。讲师还说你有二十分钟。
# en: Interlocking threads of fire hanging in the air of a lecture hall like a glowing net.
scene [827db1] = 交错的火线悬在讲堂半空，像一张发光的网。
# en: Build it slowly
opt.left.label [03433a] = 慢慢搭
# en: Your lattice is small and ugly and holds perfectly. The lecturer says "Founder-ish," which you choose to take as praise.
opt.left.say.1 [068b5a] = 你的格网又小又丑，却撑得完美无缺。讲师说“有点创始者的味道”，你决定把它当成表扬。
# en: Build it big
opt.right.label [33df52] = 搭个大的
# en: {~It's magnificent for nine seconds.|It holds just long enough for everyone to see it.} Then the strands find each other and the whole thing sighs into sparks.
opt.right.say.1 [180491] = {~它壮丽了整整九秒。|它撑得刚好够每个人看清。}然后火线彼此找到对方，整个东西叹息一声，化作火星。

@event evo_storm_pairing
# en: Storm Pairing
title [6e518e] = 风暴搭档
# en: Advanced Evocation pairs students for a storm: one calls the rain, the other the lightning, and neither is allowed to let go first. You're paired with {partner}.
text [bcffa7] = 高等塑能术让学生两两搭档召唤风暴：一人唤雨，一人引雷，谁都不许先松手。你的搭档是{partner}。
# en: Two students on a windswept tower top, one calling rain, the other calling lightning, the sky between them churning.
scene [0f5fd7] = 狂风中的塔顶上，两名学生一个唤雨一个引雷，两人之间的天空翻涌不息。
# en: Call the lightning
opt.left.label [26bb28] = 引雷
# en: The storm answers both of you at once. {partner} laughs into the wind, soaked and astonished.
opt.left.say.1 [2fb5cc] = 风暴同时回应了你们俩。{partner}迎着风大笑，浑身湿透，满脸惊愕。
# en: The lightning goes where it likes. You both spend an afternoon in the infirmary, comparing burns.
opt.left.say.2 [f7819a] = 闪电想去哪儿就去哪儿。你们俩在医务室待了一下午，互相比较烧伤。
# en: Call the rain, and let them lead
opt.right.label [f3854c] = 唤雨，让对方主导
# en: You hold the rain steady while {partner} draws the lightning down. Afterwards {they} thank{s} you for not trying to steal it.
opt.right.say.1 [be557c] = 你稳住雨幕，{partner}把闪电引了下来。之后{they}谢谢你没有抢风头。

@event evo_final_practical
# en: The Final Practical
title [035f37] = 期末实践考
# en: The last practical of Advanced Evocation: melt an ice dummy without touching the floor around it. Professor Thorne is on the panel, and he is not blinking.
text [9b1d08] = 高等塑能术的最后一场实践考：融化一个冰人偶，不许碰到周围的地面。索恩教授在考官席上，眼都不眨。
# en: An examination hall cleared of desks, a single student facing three examiners and a target dummy made of ice.
scene [49ac8b] = 清空了课桌的考场，一名学生面对三位考官和一个冰做的靶子人偶。
# en: Fire, precisely
opt.left.label [c25e11] = 用火，精准地
# en: The ice runs off the dummy and not a drop touches the floor. Thorne says "Hm," and writes something underlined.
opt.left.say.1 [0fdd37] = 冰从人偶上流下，没有一滴碰到地面。索恩说了声“嗯”，写下一行带下划线的字。
# en: The dummy melts, and so does a fair part of the floor. Thorne writes something with a question mark.
opt.left.say.2 [20fe15] = 人偶融了，地板也融了不少。索恩写下一行带问号的字。
# en: Water, patiently
opt.right.label [21c7ce] = 用水，耐心地
# en: You draw the cold out of the ice with water instead of fire. It takes twice as long. The panel watches every minute.
opt.right.say.1 [8c406a] = 你用水而不是火把冰里的寒意抽了出来。花了两倍的时间。考官们一分钟都没错过。

@event duel_first_practice
# en: First Practice
title [57e48a] = 第一次练习
# en: Lyra runs the first practice like a general. "Footwork," she says. "If your feet are wrong, your spell is a rumour." She pairs you with a dummy called Gerald the Second.
text [3c6fcf] = 莱拉像将军一样主持第一次练习。“步法，”她说，“步法错了，你的咒语就只是个传闻。”她给你配了一个叫“杰拉尔德二世”的假人。
# en: A duelling hall with chalk circles on the floor and practice dummies with names painted on their chests.
scene [f28b25] = 地上画着粉笔圈的决斗厅，练习假人胸口上漆着名字。
# en: Drill footwork
opt.left.label [7dee9f] = 练步法
# en: Two hours of stepping in circles. Gerald the Second wins every round. Your feet, however, are now correct.
opt.left.say.1 [9d28ca] = 绕圈走了两个小时。杰拉尔德二世赢了每一回合。不过你的脚，现在是对的了。
# en: Spar for real
opt.right.label [9e070e] = 真刀真枪对练
# en: You land a clean disarm on your partner. Across the hall, Lyra raises an eyebrow, which is her version of a standing ovation.
opt.right.say.1 [71d335] = 你干净利落地缴了对手的械。大厅另一头，莱拉挑了挑眉——这是她版本的起立鼓掌。
# en: You spend the evening relearning which way is up. Lyra says that's the first lesson anyway.
opt.right.say.2 [99acac] = 你一晚上都在重新学习哪边是上。莱拉说反正这本来就是第一课。

@event duel_footwork_feud
# en: The Footwork Feud
title [cf293b] = 步法之争
# en: Bram says the Circle's footwork is "Emberhall nonsense" and Lyra says Bram's footwork is "a hazard to shipping". Both of them look at you to settle it.
text [8b7ae0] = 布拉姆说决斗社的步法是“烬厅的胡闹”，莱拉说布拉姆的步法是“航运公害”。两人都看着你，等你裁决。
# en: Two students arguing in the middle of a duelling circle while the rest of the club pretends not to listen.
scene [a9dbb3] = 两名学生在决斗圈中央争吵，社里其他人假装没在听。
# en: Side with Lyra
opt.left.label [451590] = 站莱拉这边
# en: Lyra nods as if this were obvious. Bram takes a demerit book out of his pocket, looks at it, and puts it back. Progress.
opt.left.say.1 [dfa265] = 莱拉点点头，好像这是理所当然。布拉姆从口袋里掏出记过本，看了看，又放了回去。有进步。
# en: Side with Bram
opt.right.label [1bec38] = 站布拉姆这边
# en: Bram looks startled to be agreed with. Lyra looks at you like a puzzle she will solve later, with fire.
opt.right.say.1 [4720c9] = 有人赞同自己，布拉姆显得很吃惊。莱拉看你的样子，像在看一道她以后会用火来解的谜题。

@event duel_fixture
# en: Fixture Against Thornwick
title [d8c992] = 对阵荆木
# en: Thornwick Academy's duelling team has crossed the hills for a fixture. The Circle needs one more duellist in the line-up, and the captain is looking at you.
text [7ff7a2] = 荆木学院的决斗队翻山过来比赛。决斗社的阵容还差一名决斗者，社长正看着你。
# en: A duelling green with rival banners, students from both academies packed onto benches.
scene [0b0deb] = 挂着两校旗帜的决斗场，两所学院的学生挤满长凳。
# en: Duel for the Circle
opt.left.label [4b23b1] = 为决斗社出战
# en: You win your bout, and the Circle wins the fixture by a whisker. Someone carries you a few steps before remembering they don't like you.
opt.left.say.1 [8c53d7] = 你赢了自己那场，决斗社以毫厘之差赢下比赛。有人把你扛起来走了几步，才想起他们并不喜欢你。
# en: A draw. The Circle loses by one bout, but nobody blames you, and Lyra says "acceptable" twice.
opt.left.say.2 [d9fb94] = 平局。决斗社输了一场，但没人怪你，莱拉说了两遍“还行”。
# en: The Thornwick duellist is very good and very polite about it. You hate both.
opt.left.say.3 [929b7a] = 荆木的决斗者非常厉害，而且对此非常有礼貌。两样你都讨厌。
# en: Offer to be the reserve
opt.right.label [44cb08] = 主动当替补
# en: You hold coats and bring water. It turns out reserves see everything, including how Thornwick cheats.
opt.right.say.1 [eac3f5] = 你帮人拿外套、递水。原来替补什么都看得见，包括荆木是怎么作弊的。

@event duel_captain_call
# en: The Captain's Question
title [dfe526] = 社长的问题
# en: After practice, the captain sits beside you. "When I graduate, someone has to run this place," she says. "Someone who turns up. You turn up."
text [3fd3c8] = 练习结束后，社长在你身边坐下。“我毕业以后，总得有人管这地方，”她说，“得是个会准时出现的人。你会。”
# en: An empty duelling hall at night, two students sitting on the edge of a chalk circle.
scene [0d20d7] = 夜里空荡荡的决斗厅，两名学生坐在粉笔圈边上。
# en: Say you'll think about it
opt.left.label [b4769e] = 说你会考虑
# en: "Think fast," she says. "Feet first, then spells." You're fairly sure that's a yes.
opt.left.say.1 [a70c37] = “考虑快点，”她说，“先动脚，再施法。”你很确定这算是答应了。
# en: Say you're not the type
opt.right.label [9fe8f9] = 说你不是那块料
# en: "Nobody's the type," she says. "That's why it has to be someone who turns up."
opt.right.say.1 [cd23ec] = “没人是那块料，”她说，“所以才得是个会准时出现的人。”

@event lib_shelving_rush
# en: The Shelving Rush
title [5625e2] = 上架高峰
# en: Exam week, and every book in the library has been borrowed, read and returned at once. The cart is taller than you are. Footnote is sitting on top of it.
text [6fa1df] = 考试周，图书馆里的每本书都同时被借走、读完又还回来。书车比你还高。脚注正坐在最顶上。
# en: A library cart overflowing with returned books, a student pushing it at a run between towering shelves.
scene [7fe4c3] = 一辆堆满还书的图书车，一名学生推着它在高耸的书架间小跑。
# en: Shelve properly
opt.left.label [bac2cb] = 规规矩矩地上架
# en: Every book in its place by closing. Footnote has moved to the top shelf to supervise.
opt.left.say.1 [3b9e2e] = 闭馆前每本书都归了位。脚注已经挪到最高一层书架上监工了。
# en: Shelve quickly
opt.right.label [9d5012] = 快速上架
# en: The books are on shelves. Most of them are even on the right shelves. Someone will find out in a decade.
opt.right.say.1 [79d70e] = 书都在架子上了。大部分甚至在对的架子上。十年后会有人发现的。

@event lib_overdue_mage
# en: The Overdue Mage
title [99bf32] = 逾期的法师
# en: An old mage returns a book sixty years overdue and asks, with great dignity, what the fine is. The ledger says the fine is more than the library.
text [6a40d1] = 一位老法师归还一本逾期六十年的书，并十分庄重地询问罚金是多少。账本上的罚金比图书馆还值钱。
# en: An elderly mage at the library desk clutching a book that is sixty years overdue.
scene [b70648] = 一位年迈的法师站在图书馆柜台前，紧攥着一本逾期六十年的书。
# en: Waive it
opt.left.label [899866] = 免了吧
# en: The old mage thanks you and leaves a sweet on the desk. Later you find out he taught Professor Thorne.
opt.left.say.1 [ef4397] = 老法师谢过你，在柜台上留下一颗糖。后来你才知道，他教过索恩教授。
# en: Charge it, by the book
opt.right.label [396965] = 照章收费
# en: The mage pays in coins so old the bank has to look them up. The head librarian is delighted.
opt.right.say.1 [6746d8] = 法师付的硬币老到银行都得去查。馆长高兴坏了。

@event lib_footnote_strike
# en: Footnote Goes on Strike
title [ec48a4] = 脚注罢工
# en: Footnote has lain down across the reference desk and will not move. Students are queueing. The cat has made its demands clear: none.
text [8627c8] = 脚注横躺在参考咨询台上，一动不动。学生们在排队。这只猫已经把它的诉求表达得很清楚了：没有诉求。
# en: A large library cat lying across a reference desk, refusing to move, while students queue in front of it.
scene [bcfc48] = 一只大个儿的图书馆猫横躺在参考咨询台上不肯挪窝，学生们在它面前排起了队。
# en: Bribe him with fish
opt.left.label [ca7565] = 用鱼贿赂它
# en: Footnote accepts the fish, the apology and the chair you bring him. The queue resumes.
opt.left.say.1 [d9ebb3] = 脚注接受了鱼、道歉，还有你搬来的椅子。队伍恢复了流动。
# en: Work around him
opt.right.label [ea0c37] = 绕开它干活
# en: You stamp books on the far end of the desk for an hour. Footnote watches with the calm of a cat who has won.
opt.right.say.1 [40e4a9] = 你在柜台另一头盖了一小时的章。脚注以胜利者的平静注视着你。

@event court_fountain_freeze
# en: The Frozen Fountain
title [f87a8e] = 冻住的喷泉
# en: The courtyard fountain has frozen in the middle of a splash. The water hangs in the air like glass. A first-year is trying to lick it.
text [abc188] = 庭院的喷泉在水花溅起的一瞬冻住了。水像玻璃一样悬在半空。一个一年级生正想去舔它。
# en: A courtyard fountain frozen mid-splash, the water hanging in the air like glass.
scene [8a0a42] = 庭院喷泉冻在了水花飞溅的瞬间，水像玻璃一样悬在空中。
# en: Stop the first-year
opt.left.label [d24736] = 拦住那个一年级生
# en: You pull the first-year away just as the ice cracks. For a moment you'd swear you saw a black star reflected in it.
opt.left.say.1 [267623] = 冰裂开的那一刻，你正好把一年级生拉开。有一瞬间，你发誓看见冰里映着一颗黑色的星。
# en: Study the ice
opt.right.label [e6dcae] = 研究这块冰
# en: The ice is colder than ice should be. Your notes say "colder than ice should be" three times.
opt.right.say.1 [3744c0] = 这冰比冰该有的还冷。你的笔记里把“比冰该有的还冷”写了三遍。

@event court_rumour_mill
# en: The Rumour Mill
title [b2db14] = 流言工坊
# en: {gossip} has news, which is to say gossip, which is to say three different stories about the same broken window. "You'll want to hear this," {they} say{s}.
text [ba7e30] = {gossip}有新闻——也就是八卦——也就是关于同一扇破窗户的三个不同版本。“你会想听的，”{they}说。
# en: Students huddled around the courtyard fountain trading whispers, one of them clearly enjoying it most.
scene [bc5c84] = 学生们围在庭院喷泉边交换耳语，其中一个显然最乐在其中。
# en: Listen to all of it
opt.left.label [71c08a] = 全都听一遍
# en: You hear all three stories. Two are true. One is about you.
opt.left.say.1 [1839fa] = 三个版本你都听了。两个是真的。一个是关于你的。
# en: Make up a better one
opt.right.label [ed234b] = 编个更好的
# en: Your story is better than all three. By dinner it's the official version.
opt.right.say.1 [2aa741] = 你的版本比那三个都好。到晚饭时，它已经成了官方说法。

@event lake_skimming
# en: Skimming Stones
title [a14e0e] = 打水漂
# en: {friend} is skimming stones on the Mirror Lake. The water is so still each stone leaves rings that go on forever. "Seven," {they} say{s}. "Beat that."
text [90f788] = {friend}在镜湖上打水漂。湖面静得出奇，每块石头留下的涟漪都仿佛永远不会散。“七下，”{they}说，“来比比。”
# en: Two students skimming stones across a perfectly still lake at dusk.
scene [d7fdb5] = 黄昏时分，两名学生在一片静止如镜的湖面上打水漂。
# en: Try to beat it
opt.left.label [1284ba] = 试着赢过去
# en: Nine skips. {friend} demands a rematch and gets one. The afternoon disappears into stones.
opt.left.say.1 [1f9fa1] = 九下。{friend}要求再来一局，也如愿了。整个下午都消失在石子里。
# en: Your stone sinks with great dignity. {friend} laughs until {they} have to sit down.
opt.left.say.2 [533d65] = 你的石头带着极大的尊严沉了下去。{friend}笑得只好坐下来。
# en: Just watch the rings
opt.right.label [39fffc] = 就看涟漪
# en: You sit and watch the rings spread until the light goes. Neither of you says much. It's one of the good afternoons.
opt.right.say.1 [2ebf1f] = 你坐着看涟漪扩散，直到天光散尽。你们俩都没说什么。这是那种美好的下午之一。

@event lake_reflection_bet
# en: The Reflection Bet
title [7b2fea] = 倒影的赌约
# en: Your reflection in the Mirror Lake is holding a coin you don't have. It flips it. It catches it. It offers it to you.
text [ad0e65] = 你在镜湖里的倒影拿着一枚你并没有的硬币。它抛起，接住，然后递向你。
# en: A student staring into a still lake where their reflection appears to be holding a coin.
scene [407b4a] = 一名学生凝视着平静的湖面，水中的倒影似乎握着一枚硬币。
# en: Take the coin
opt.left.label [4cb026] = 接过硬币
# en: The coin is real, and cold, and you can't remember putting it in your pocket.
opt.left.say.1 [67628e] = 硬币是真的，冰凉，而你想不起自己是什么时候把它放进口袋的。
# en: Shake your head
opt.right.label [5e0346] = 摇头
# en: Your reflection shrugs, pockets the coin and walks out of the frame before you do.
opt.right.say.1 [3c806f] = 你的倒影耸耸肩，把硬币揣进兜里，先你一步走出了画面。

@event ref_food_fight
# en: Pudding Diplomacy
title [f97acc] = 布丁外交
# en: A pudding sails across the refectory and lands in Bram's lap. The hall goes silent. Every eye turns to the table it came from, which is yours.
text [e5a752] = 一块布丁飞过膳堂，落在布拉姆腿上。大厅一片死寂。所有目光都转向它飞来的那张桌子——你的那张。
# en: A refectory mid-food-fight, puddings in the air, a prefect rising slowly from behind a table.
scene [b7e5a2] = 膳堂里一场食物大战正酣，布丁在空中飞，一位级长从桌子后面缓缓站起。
# en: Own up
opt.left.label [3a0128] = 承认是我
# en: Bram writes you a demerit, then pauses. "Good throw," he says, almost without wanting to.
opt.left.say.1 [d32724] = 布拉姆给你记了一次过，然后顿了顿。“扔得好，”他说，几乎是不情愿的。
# en: Throw another
opt.right.label [7417cc] = 再扔一块
# en: The second pudding starts a war that the refectory will talk about for years. Historians will argue about who won. You know.
opt.right.say.1 [2e4f89] = 第二块布丁引发了一场膳堂会议论好几年的战争。史学家会争论谁赢了。你知道。

@event ref_cook_secret
# en: The Cook's Secret
title [c0a5b6] = 厨娘的秘密
# en: The cook catches you lingering by the kitchen door. "You look like someone who misses proper soup," she says, and hands you a bowl before you can deny it.
text [1cf0fd] = 厨娘逮到你在厨房门口徘徊。“你看着就像个想念正经汤的人，”她说，不等你否认就递来一碗。
# en: A huge kitchen behind the refectory, an enormous cook stirring a pot with a spoon the size of an oar.
scene [ea98ca] = 膳堂后面的大厨房，一位魁梧的厨娘用船桨那么大的勺子搅着锅。
# en: Eat it slowly
opt.left.label [3da080] = 慢慢地喝
# en: It tastes like the kitchen at home. You don't say so. She can tell anyway.
opt.left.say.1 [d6f79e] = 这味道像家里的厨房。你没说出口。她反正看得出来。
# en: Ask for the recipe
opt.right.label [604f64] = 讨要配方
# en: "Ha," says the cook, which means no, which means you'll have to keep coming back.
opt.right.say.1 [fdb0a2] = “哈，”厨娘说。意思是不行，也就是说你得一直回来。

@event obs_comet_watch
# en: The Comet Watch
title [d479ab] = 守望彗星
# en: A comet is due tonight and the observatory is full of students pretending they came for the science. The telescope has a queue. The roof has a view.
text [20d293] = 今晚有彗星经过，观星台里挤满了假装是为科学而来的学生。望远镜前排着队。屋顶上有好风景。
# en: The brass dome of an observatory open to the night, a student at the eyepiece, another beside them with a notebook.
scene [3227ec] = 向夜空敞开的黄铜穹顶观星台，一名学生凑在目镜前，另一人拿着笔记本站在旁边。
# en: Queue for the telescope
opt.left.label [1a7ef0] = 排队用望远镜
# en: Your turn at the eyepiece lasts thirty seconds. The comet's tail is green. You'll remember it longer than most lectures.
opt.left.say.1 [54f31c] = 轮到你看目镜只有三十秒。彗尾是绿色的。你会记得它比大多数课都久。
# en: Watch from the roof
opt.right.label [5e0cfb] = 去屋顶看
# en: The comet crosses the sky slowly, like it's looking for something. Kael is already on the roof. He moves over to make room.
opt.right.say.1 [344326] = 彗星慢慢划过天空，像在找什么东西。凯尔已经在屋顶上了。他挪了挪，给你让出位置。

@event obs_star_chart
# en: The Missing Star
title [f95144] = 缺失的星
# en: An old star chart in the observatory archive has a circle drawn where a star should be, with a note in faded ink: "It eats the light. Do not chart it."
text [f9ab12] = 观星台档案里一张旧星图上，本该是一颗星的地方画着一个圈，旁边用褪色的墨水写着：“它吞噬光。勿绘。”
# en: An old star chart spread on a desk, one constellation with a careful empty circle drawn where a star should be.
scene [8cbcfa] = 桌上摊开一张旧星图，某个星座里本该有星的位置被仔细地画了一个空圈。
# en: Copy the chart
opt.left.label [ddb5f3] = 抄下星图
# en: You copy it carefully. That night you dream of a circle with nothing inside it, waiting.
opt.left.say.1 [c900a1] = 你仔细地抄了下来。那晚你梦见一个空无一物的圈，在等待。
# en: Put it back
opt.right.label [862ed2] = 放回原处
# en: You return it to the drawer. The drawer feels colder when you close it.
opt.right.say.1 [ca8bc6] = 你把它放回抽屉。合上时，抽屉似乎冷了些。

@event green_mandrake_choir
# en: The Mandrake Choir
title [a16982] = 曼德拉草合唱团
# en: Tobias has taught the greenhouse mandrakes to scream in harmony. He would like your opinion. The mandrakes would like an audience.
text [26476f] = 托比亚斯教会了温室里的曼德拉草用和声尖叫。他想听听你的意见。曼德拉草想要观众。
# en: A greenhouse bench of potted mandrakes wearing tiny earmuffs, a student conducting them with a pencil.
scene [556372] = 温室长凳上一排戴着小耳罩的盆栽曼德拉草，一名学生拿铅笔指挥它们。
# en: Conduct a verse
opt.left.label [8d7d71] = 指挥一段
# en: You conduct one verse. Your ears ring for a day. Tobias says it's the best performance they've given.
opt.left.say.1 [fe14aa] = 你指挥了一段。耳朵嗡嗡响了一整天。托比亚斯说这是它们最好的一场演出。
# en: Wear earmuffs and listen
opt.right.label [fa6dc3] = 戴上耳罩听
# en: Through the earmuffs it sounds almost beautiful. Tobias is so proud he cries a little.
opt.right.say.1 [07ed14] = 隔着耳罩，听起来几乎很美。托比亚斯骄傲得哭了一小会儿。

@event green_moonflower_sprout
# en: A Moonflower Seedling
title [e51a03] = 月光花幼苗
# en: In a forgotten corner of the greenhouse, a moonflower seed has sprouted on its own, eleven years early. It glows faintly when you lean over it.
text [b895be] = 温室一个被遗忘的角落里，一粒月光花种子自己发了芽，早了整整十一年。你俯身靠近时，它发出微弱的光。
# en: A tiny silver-leaved seedling in a clay pot, glowing faintly in a dark greenhouse.
scene [1fd66d] = 陶盆里一株银叶小苗，在黑暗的温室中幽幽发光。
# en: Pot it and look after it
opt.left.label [aa4dfe] = 移进盆里好好照料
# en: You give it a pot, a label and a name. It glows a little brighter when you visit.
opt.left.say.1 [3976bb] = 你给了它一个盆、一张标签和一个名字。你来看它时，它会亮一点。
# en: Tell Tobias
opt.right.label [fe6832] = 告诉托比亚斯
# en: Tobias is speechless, then very loud. The seedling gets a sign, a fence and a rota.
opt.right.say.1 [69881e] = 托比亚斯先是说不出话，然后非常大声。幼苗得到了一块牌子、一圈篱笆和一张值班表。

@event castle_empty_halls
# en: Empty Halls
title [468042] = 空荡的走廊
# en: The castle in the holidays is enormous and quiet. Your footsteps echo down corridors you've never been alone in. A door you've never noticed is standing open.
text [30fae9] = 假期里的城堡巨大而安静。你的脚步声在从没独自走过的走廊里回荡。一扇你从未注意过的门敞开着。
# en: A long castle corridor in the holidays, dust in sunbeams, one student walking alone.
scene [c48035] = 假期里一条长长的城堡走廊，阳光里浮着灰尘，一名学生独自走着。
# en: Go through the door
opt.left.label [974ffb] = 穿过那扇门
# en: It leads to a stair that leads to a locked door that leads, you're almost sure, to the seventh tower.
opt.left.say.1 [6544d0] = 门后是一段楼梯，楼梯通向一扇锁着的门，而那扇门——你几乎可以肯定——通向第七塔。
# en: Read in the window seat
opt.right.label [a83ff6] = 在窗边座位上读书
# en: You read all day in a window seat with the whole lake below you. The best kind of nothing.
opt.right.say.1 [19769a] = 你在窗边座位上读了一整天书，整片湖就在脚下。最好的那种无所事事。

@event castle_skeleton_crew
# en: The Skeleton Crew
title [6ec6d4] = 留守的人们
# en: Supper in the holidays is one table in the Great Hall: you, three other students, the cook, two prefects and Old Maud, who has brought her goat.
text [a9be7b] = 假期的晚饭只在大礼堂摆一张桌子：你、另外三个学生、厨娘、两位级长，还有带着山羊来的老莫德。
# en: A handful of staff and students sharing a long table in a nearly empty great hall.
scene [4c6b8f] = 几乎空荡的大礼堂里，寥寥几名职员和学生共用一张长桌。
# en: Sit next to Maud
opt.left.label [d82b60] = 坐在莫德旁边
# en: Maud tells a story about the frozen spring that she's never told the term-time students. Bartholomew eats your napkin.
opt.left.say.1 [2c57bf] = 莫德讲了一个关于冰封之春的故事，那是她从没对学期里的学生讲过的。巴塞洛缪吃掉了你的餐巾。
# en: Play cards with the prefects
opt.right.label [a22285] = 和级长们打牌
# en: The prefects play cards like they enforce rules: badly and with great confidence. You win dessert.
opt.right.say.1 [3b59a8] = 级长们打牌就像执行校规：水平很烂，信心十足。你赢了甜点。

@event home_family_supper
# en: Supper at Home
title [1f26c6] = 家里的晚饭
# en: Supper at home. Everyone wants to know what you've learned. You try to explain evocation to an aunt who thinks it's a kind of cheese.
text [8ab73f] = 家里的晚饭。每个人都想知道你学了什么。你试着向一位以为塑能术是某种奶酪的姑妈解释它。
# en: A crowded kitchen table, a family passing dishes, a student back from the academy being asked too many questions.
scene [ec2a5f] = 挤满人的餐桌，一家人传着菜，一个从学院回来的学生被问了太多问题。
# en: Show them a spell
opt.left.label [803b4f] = 给他们露一手
# en: You light every candle in the room at once. Your aunt applauds and asks if you can do it with cheese.
opt.left.say.1 [5d4fe6] = 你一下点亮了屋里所有的蜡烛。姑妈鼓掌，问你能不能对奶酪也来一下。
# en: Just listen
opt.right.label [6a9f3e] = 就听着
# en: You let them talk. You'd forgotten how loud and how good it is.
opt.right.say.1 [738cc0] = 你让他们说。你都忘了这有多吵，又有多好。

@event home_old_friend
# en: An Old Friend
title [8809c5] = 老朋友
# en: Your oldest friend is sitting on the wall at the edge of the fields, exactly where you left them. "So," they say. "Are you a wizard now, or what?"
text [e85e1a] = 你最老的朋友坐在田边的矮墙上，就在你离开时的那个位置。“所以，”对方说，“你现在算巫师了，还是怎样？”
# en: Two old friends sitting on a field wall at sunset, one in academy robes, the other in work clothes.
scene [82fd45] = 夕阳下两位老朋友坐在田边矮墙上，一个穿着学院长袍，另一个穿着干活的衣服。
# en: Tell them everything
opt.left.label [09f8b1] = 把一切都告诉对方
# en: You talk until the stars come out. They want to hear about the lake most of all.
opt.left.say.1 [5d2429] = 你们一直聊到星星出来。对方最想听的是那片湖。
# en: Ask about their life instead
opt.right.label [24a3a1] = 反过来问问对方的生活
# en: They've been busy too: a farm, a fiancé, a goat that bites. Your life isn't the only one that grew.
opt.right.say.1 [91a591] = 对方也很忙：一座农场、一位未婚夫、一只咬人的山羊。长大的不只是你的生活。

@event home_market_day
# en: Market Day
title [0bcdaf] = 赶集日
# en: Market day in town. A stallholder recognises your academy robes and asks if you can do anything about his leaky roof. For a price.
text [ebfea1] = 镇上的赶集日。一个摊主认出了你的学院长袍，问你能不能帮他修修漏雨的屋顶。有偿的。
# en: A small country market, a student in academy robes being stared at by stallholders.
scene [a7a658] = 一个乡间小集市，一名穿着学院长袍的学生被摊主们盯着看。
# en: Fix it with magic
opt.left.label [77d22c] = 用魔法修好它
# en: The roof is dry, the stallholder is thrilled and you are slightly scorched. He pays in apples and coins.
opt.left.say.1 [f09cd8] = 屋顶干了，摊主乐坏了，你被轻微烤焦了。他用苹果和硬币付账。
# en: Just buy sweets
opt.right.label [bbf438] = 只买糖
# en: The sweet shop still sells your favourites. You eat them on the bridge like you used to.
opt.right.say.1 [ea94aa] = 糖果店还卖你最爱的那几样。你像从前一样坐在桥上吃。

@event work_double_shift
# en: The Double Shift
title [6df679] = 连轴转
# en: Holiday shifts pay double and feel triple. It's your second shift today and the evening rush hasn't started.
text [60fdf7] = 假期的班工钱翻倍，感觉翻三倍。这是你今天的第二个班，晚高峰还没开始。
# en: A student asleep on their feet behind a counter, a clock on the wall showing a very late hour.
scene [6bbbbe] = 一名学生站在柜台后面睡着了，墙上的钟指着一个很晚的时间。
# en: Push through
opt.left.label [f6ed7c] = 咬牙撑过去
# en: You push through. The coins are heavy in your pocket and your feet are heavy everywhere else.
opt.left.say.1 [900c8d] = 你撑过去了。口袋里的硬币沉甸甸的，身上其他地方也沉甸甸的。
# en: Swap the shift
opt.right.label [dcf3f9] = 找人换班
# en: A colleague takes it for a favour you'll owe later. You sleep for eleven hours.
opt.right.say.1 [6106e9] = 一位同事替了你，换你以后欠一个人情。你睡了十一个小时。

@event intern_first_assignment
# en: The First Assignment
title [12864b] = 第一项任务
# en: Your supervisor at the Royal Library hands you a list of forty uncatalogued boxes. "Find out what's in them," she says. "Carefully. One of them is probably alive."
text [106ac0] = 你在皇家图书馆的导师递给你一张清单，上面是四十个未编目的箱子。“查清里面有什么，”她说，“小心点。其中有一个大概是活的。”
# en: A vast underground archive, a supervisor handing a student a list longer than their arm.
scene [cf395e] = 一座巨大的地下档案馆，导师递给学生一张比胳膊还长的清单。
# en: Work through the boxes
opt.left.label [af7cdf] = 逐个整理箱子
# en: Box thirty-one is alive. It's a very small, very old dictionary that bites. You catalogue it.
opt.left.say.1 [f9f573] = 第三十一号箱是活的。里面是一本很小、很老、会咬人的词典。你把它编了目。
# en: Ask the other interns
opt.right.label [d7f73e] = 问问其他实习生
# en: The other interns have a system, a rota and a song. You learn all three.
opt.right.say.1 [b61185] = 其他实习生有一套系统、一张值班表和一首歌。三样你都学会了。

@event intern_index_maze
# en: The Index Maze
title [708be7] = 索引迷宫
# en: A cross-reference in the archive leads to another, and another, and another, deeper under the city. The last card is about the founders of Lumenhold.
text [6ca7e0] = 档案里的一条交叉引用指向另一条，又一条，再一条，越来越深地钻进城市地下。最后一张卡片讲的是流明堡的创始者。
# en: A student lost between endless shelves underground, following an index card trail by lamplight.
scene [37ed2d] = 一名学生迷失在地下无尽的书架间，借着灯光追寻一串索引卡的线索。
# en: Follow it to the end
opt.left.label [b0b834] = 追到底
# en: At the end is a letter from a founder about "the seventh lock". You copy it with shaking hands.
opt.left.say.1 [89da61] = 尽头是一位创始者写的信，谈到“第七把锁”。你手发着抖把它抄了下来。
# en: The trail ends at a missing card. Somebody took it. Recently.
opt.left.say.2 [a4b290] = 线索断在一张缺失的卡片上。有人拿走了它。就在最近。
# en: Report it to your supervisor
opt.right.label [10c4be] = 报告给导师
# en: Your supervisor reads the card, goes pale and writes a letter to the headmistress of Lumenhold.
opt.right.say.1 [10b589] = 导师读了卡片，脸色发白，提笔给流明堡的院长写了封信。

@event thesis_proposal
# en: The Proposal
title [0d98d2] = 开题
# en: Your thesis proposal is due. Professor Thorne wants one sentence that says what you'll find out. You have eleven sentences and none of them is it.
text [6735b0] = 论文开题报告该交了。索恩教授要一句话，说清你要查明什么。你有十一句话，没有一句是。
# en: A desk covered in drafts, one page with a single sentence circled many times.
scene [19addc] = 一张铺满草稿的桌子，有一页上只有一句话，被圈了很多遍。
# en: Rewrite it all night
opt.left.label [2fa9ed] = 通宵重写
# en: At dawn you have one sentence. Thorne reads it twice. "Yes," he says. "That."
opt.left.say.1 [348567] = 黎明时你有了一句话。索恩读了两遍。“对，”他说，“就是这个。”
# en: Hand in what you have
opt.right.label [648c9a] = 交上手头的
# en: Thorne reads all eleven sentences and circles the fourth. "That one," he says. "Next time, only that one."
opt.right.say.1 [8b0a3c] = 索恩读完十一句话，圈出第四句。“这一句，”他说，“下次，只要这一句。”

@event thesis_lab_night
# en: Late in the Lab
title [d2c7a0] = 实验室深夜
# en: The thesis lab after midnight: everyone else has gone home, and your argument has a hole in it the size of the seventh tower.
text [0fcfb7] = 午夜后的论文实验室：其他人都回去了，而你的论证里有一个第七塔那么大的漏洞。
# en: A thesis laboratory at midnight, one carrel lit, a student surrounded by open books.
scene [9ec7f2] = 午夜的论文实验室，只有一个隔间亮着灯，一名学生被摊开的书围着。
# en: Find the hole
opt.left.label [35b489] = 找到漏洞
# en: You find it, fill it and find two more. That's progress, apparently.
opt.left.say.1 [e36cbd] = 你找到了，补上了，又发现了两个。据说这就叫进展。
# en: Go to bed
opt.right.label [2fa817] = 去睡觉
# en: You sleep. In the morning the hole is still there, but you can see the edges of it.
opt.right.say.1 [0eb578] = 你睡了。早上漏洞还在，但你能看清它的边了。

@event bell_first_ring
# en: A Bell Under the Water
title [1289ef] = 水下的钟声
# en: In the middle of the night you hear a bell, low and slow, from the middle of the lake. Nobody else in your dormitory wakes up.
text [cfa605] = 半夜里你听见钟声，低沉而缓慢，从湖心传来。宿舍里没有别人醒来。
# en: A dark lakeshore at night, ripples spreading from the middle of the lake though nothing has fallen in.
scene [38d9e1] = 夜里漆黑的湖岸，涟漪从湖心扩散开来，尽管什么都没有落进水里。
# en: Go down to the shore
opt.left.label [c0c878] = 下到湖边去
# en: The water is perfectly still. Then, once, a ring spreads out from the centre, as if the lake had been struck from below.
opt.left.say.1 [baf151] = 湖面纹丝不动。然后，只一次，一圈涟漪从中心荡开，仿佛湖被人从下面敲了一下。
# en: Pull the blanket over your head
opt.right.label [352adf] = 把毯子蒙过头
# en: It rings seven times. You count every one. In the morning you are the only one who remembers.
opt.right.say.1 [e7bc35] = 钟响了七下。你每一下都数了。到了早上，只有你一个人还记得。

@event bell_maud_rope
# en: Maud's Rope
title [852d20] = 莫德的绳子
# en: {keeper} shows you a rope, frayed and black with lake water, that she's kept in her shed for sixty years. "From the bell," she says. "It came up the night the lake froze. Someone cut it."
text [090813] = {keeper}给你看一根绳子，磨损了，被湖水浸得发黑，她在棚子里留了六十年。“钟上的，”她说，“湖冻上那晚它浮了上来。有人割断了它。”
# en: An old woman in a garden shed holding up a frayed, waterlogged bell-rope.
scene [609899] = 花园棚屋里，一位老妇人举着一根磨损、浸透了水的钟绳。
# en: Ask who cut it
opt.left.label [a6108f] = 问是谁割断的
# en: "That," says {keeper}, "is the question I've been asking for sixty years." She promises to tell you what she knows, when she's ready.
opt.left.say.1 [4bd3a1] = “这个嘛，”{keeper}说，“我问了六十年了。”她答应等她准备好，就把知道的告诉你。
# en: Leave her to her memories
opt.right.label [9f94d2] = 让她独自回忆
# en: You leave her with the rope in her lap. She doesn't notice you go.
opt.right.say.1 [10a7b7] = 你留她抱着膝上的绳子。她没注意到你离开。

@event bell_answer
# en: What Maud Remembers
title [7f91ce] = 莫德记得的事
# en: {npc} finds you by the boathouse. "The rope," she says. "Edmund cut it. To stop the bell ringing the thing awake. It went on ringing anyway."
text [b0e638] = {npc}在船屋边找到你。“那根绳子，”她说，“是埃德蒙割的。为了不让钟声把那东西敲醒。可钟还是一直在响。”
# en: An old woman and a student sitting by a cottage fire, a waterlogged rope coiled between them.
scene [6145b3] = 小屋炉火边坐着一位老妇人和一名学生，两人之间盘着一根浸透水的绳子。
# en: Listen
opt.ok.label [03cec6] = 听着
# en: She talks until the light goes. When she's finished, she seems lighter, and you seem to be carrying something.
opt.ok.say.1 [de8d6c] = 她一直讲到天光散尽。讲完时她似乎轻松了，而你似乎背上了什么。

@event bell_drowned
# en: The Diving Bell
title [980982] = 潜水钟
# en: The bell has rung every night for a week. The boathouse has an old diving helmet and a rope. The lake is very dark and very still.
text [62e2e6] = 钟已经连着响了一个星期。船屋里有一个旧潜水头盔和一根绳子。湖水非常黑，非常静。
# en: A student in a borrowed diving helmet standing at the end of a jetty over black water.
scene [f56404] = 一名学生戴着借来的潜水头盔，站在黑水之上的栈桥尽头。
# en: Dive
opt.left.label [ad77f7] = 潜下去
# en: Far down, the bell lies on its side, and around its rim, letters: a name you don't know. You surface gasping, and you keep the name.
opt.left.say.1 [f03244] = 在很深的地方，钟侧躺着，钟沿上刻着字：一个你不认识的名字。你喘着气浮出水面，把那个名字记在了心里。
# en: The cold drives you back up before you see anything. Old Maud is waiting on the jetty with a blanket and a look.
opt.left.say.2 [32863f] = 你还没看见什么，寒冷就把你逼了回去。老莫德拿着毯子和一个眼神等在栈桥上。
# en: Wait for the bell to stop
opt.right.label [d2920e] = 等钟声停下
# en: You wait for a week. It doesn't stop. Something in you decides it will have to be you, next time.
opt.right.say.1 [717419] = 你等了一个星期。它没有停。你心里有什么东西决定了：下一次，得是你去。

@event bell_silence
# en: The Bell Falls Silent
title [6d5cb4] = 钟声沉寂
# en: {clue(bell_name): You say the name from the bell's rim out loud, over the water.|You stand at the shore with Maud's rope in your hands.} The bell rings one last time, and then the lake is just a lake.
text [721f49] = {clue(bell_name): 你对着湖面，大声念出钟沿上的那个名字。|你站在岸边，手里握着莫德的绳子。}钟最后响了一次，然后湖就只是一片湖了。
# en: The Mirror Lake at dawn, perfectly still, a student standing at the water's edge with a lantern.
scene [82908a] = 黎明的镜湖，平静如镜，一名学生提着灯站在水边。
# en: Let it rest
opt.ok.label [657b8b] = 让它安息
# en: For the first time in sixty years, the lake is quiet. Somewhere in her cottage, you think, Maud sleeps through the night.
opt.ok.say.1 [e9634e] = 六十年来第一次，湖安静了下来。你想，此刻在小屋里，莫德一定一觉睡到了天亮。
